.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead policy" 1  "bead policy " 
.SH NAME
bead policy \- Validate workspace policy and scheduling configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead policy\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lint scheduling and retention configuration.
.PP
Policy lint is advisory only: it reports contradictory, unreachable, redundant,
or ineffective settings and never changes whether a bead is claimable.
.PP
  bead policy check [\-\-format text|json]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bead policy\-check(1)
Validate workspace policy and scheduling configuration
.TP
bead policy\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
